WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.362
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.662 --> 00:00:09.118
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:14.462
Unit six: Future with 'going to'. Today you will talk about plans and intentions.

4
00:00:14.762 --> 00:00:17.379
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:21.659
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.517 --> 00:00:23.622
Going to.

7
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:26.941
Going to means used to talk about plans.

8
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.934
I am going to study.

9
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.877
Your turn. Say: Going to.

10
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:35.827
Going to.

11
00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:37.306
Plan.

12
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:40.560
Plan means an idea about what you will do.

13
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:42.836
My plan is to travel.

14
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.766
Your turn. Say: Plan.

15
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.404
Plan.

16
00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.128
Intention.

17
00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:55.173
Intention means something that you want and plan to do.

18
00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:58.096
My intention is to pass the exam.

19
00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:01.440
Your turn. Say: Intention.

20
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.289
Intention.

21
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:06.796
Tomorrow.

22
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:09.957
Tomorrow means the day after today.

23
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.271
I am going to rest tomorrow.

24
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:15.640
Your turn. Say: Tomorrow.

25
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.431
Tomorrow.

26
00:01:20.183 --> 00:01:21.150
Next week.

27
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:24.150
Next week means the week after this one.

28
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.680
We are going to travel next week.

29
00:01:27.283 --> 00:01:29.889
Your turn. Say: Next week.

30
00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:33.920
Next week.

31
00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:35.696
Decide.

32
00:01:36.683 --> 00:01:38.753
Decide means to choose what to do.

33
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.338
I decided to study abroad.

34
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.254
Your turn. Say: Decide.

35
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.171
Decide.

36
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:49.906
Prepare.

37
00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:53.148
Prepare means to get ready for something.

38
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.390
We prepare for the test.

39
00:01:55.983 --> 00:01:58.438
Your turn. Say: Prepare.

40
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.231
Prepare.

41
00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:03.868
Future.

42
00:02:04.883 --> 00:02:06.778
Future means the time that will come.

43
00:02:07.383 --> 00:02:08.942
I think about my future.

44
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.877
Your turn. Say: Future.

45
00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:15.618
Future.

46
00:02:16.433 --> 00:02:19.968
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.817 --> 00:02:23.083
Visal, what are you going to do next week?

48
00:02:24.183 --> 00:02:33.105
I am going to visit my cousin. We use be + going to + base verb for plans and intentions that we have already decided.

49
00:02:34.217 --> 00:02:35.589
And for predictions?

50
00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:45.039
We also use it when we see evidence now: Look at the clouds! It is going to rain. The evidence is in front of us, so we are sure.

51
00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.766
How do we ask and answer?

52
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:57.489
Are you going to come? Yes, I am. No, I'm not. What are you going to do? We write going to but we often say gonna in fast speech.

53
00:02:58.633 --> 00:03:00.366
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.217 --> 00:03:05.248
Grammar focus: Future: be plus going to plus base verb.

55
00:03:05.548 --> 00:03:06.700
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.383 --> 00:03:09.812
I am going to visit my cousin next week.

57
00:03:10.717 --> 00:03:13.065
She is going to prepare for the test.

58
00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.450
It is going to rain soon.

59
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:24.532
Use be going to + base verb for plans and for predictions based on evidence. Questions: Are you going to…? Negative: am / is / are not going to.

60
00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:28.423
Be careful! Don't say: She going to cook tonight.

61
00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.958
Say: She is going to cook tonight.

62
00:03:33.258 --> 00:03:34.944
Add is before going to.

63
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:38.281
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:40.439
Plans for the Future.

65
00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:43.610
Next week I am going to visit my cousin in Battambang.

66
00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:49.316
My sister has decided to study medicine, so she is going to prepare for the exam.

67
00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.952
Look at the sky! It is going to rain.

68
00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.850
We are not going to play football today.

69
00:03:56.867 --> 00:03:58.889
Everyone has a plan for the future.

70
00:03:60.000 --> 00:04:04.234
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.083 --> 00:04:06.932
I blank going to study tonight.

72
00:04:07.232 --> 00:04:10.108
A, am. B, is. C, are.

73
00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.144
The answer is A: am.

74
00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:18.004
They are going to blank tomorrow.

75
00:04:18.304 --> 00:04:21.702
A, travelled. B, travel. C, travelling.

76
00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:27.255
The answer is B: travel.

77
00:04:28.417 --> 00:04:31.115
Look at the clouds! It blank rain.

78
00:04:31.415 --> 00:04:35.498
A, is going to. B, will to. C, goes to.

79
00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:41.103
The answer is A: is going to.

80
00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:43.959
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:44.259 --> 00:04:48.923
A, She going to cook.. B, She is going to cook.. C, She is go to cook..

82
00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:55.291
The answer is B: She is going to cook..

83
00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:59.901
According to the reading, what is the writer's sister going to study?

84
00:05:00.201 --> 00:05:03.262
A, medicine. B, law. C, art.

85
00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.718
The answer is A: medicine.

86
00:05:09.933 --> 00:05:13.294
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:15.790
What are you going to do next week?

88
00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:26.026
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:39.639
Next week I am going to visit my grandmother in Battambang. We are going to cook together and walk around the market. I am also going to study for my English test, because I want to get a good result.

90
00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.741
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:48.646
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future: be plus going to plus base verb.

92
00:05:48.946 --> 00:05:53.967
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:56.908
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

94
00:05:57.208 --> 00:05:59.802
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

